# --- @fill: weather frames ----------------------------------------------------
# Weather is this lesson's centerpiece. Distractors are sibling weather adjectives
# the learner already knows, forcing discrimination between similar states.

@fill
@lu Et ass [sonneg] an et ass waarm.
@en It is [sunny] and it is warm.
@distractor-lu bedeckt
@distractor-lu niwweleg
@distractor-lu donkel
@distractor-en cloudy
@distractor-en foggy
@distractor-en dark

@fill
@lu D'Luucht ass [hell] an d'Kichen ass grouss.
@en The lamp is [bright] and the kitchen is big.
@distractor-lu donkel
@distractor-lu kuerz
@distractor-lu bëlleg
@distractor-en dark
@distractor-en short
@distractor-en cheap

@fill
@lu Et ass [bedeckt] an et reent e bëssen.
@en It is [cloudy] and it is raining a bit.
@distractor-lu sonneg
@distractor-lu niwweleg
@distractor-lu waarm
@distractor-en sunny
@distractor-en foggy
@distractor-en warm

@fill
@lu Et ass [niwweleg] an ech gesinn net vill.
@en It is [foggy] and I do not see much.
@distractor-lu bedeckt
@distractor-lu sonneg
@distractor-lu donkel
@distractor-en cloudy
@distractor-en sunny
@distractor-en dark

# --- @fill: predicative adjectives with sinn/ass ------------------------------
# The learner sees the frame with the subject + copula and picks the adjective.
# Distractors are other adjectives from this lesson, all plausible in context.

@fill
@lu D'Stuff ass [grouss] an d'Kichen ass kleng.
@en The living room is [big] and the kitchen is small.
@distractor-lu schéin
@distractor-lu nei
@distractor-lu al
@distractor-en beautiful
@distractor-en new
@distractor-en old

@fill
@lu Dat Bett ass [nei] an d'Couche ass al.
@en That bed is [new] and the sofa is old.
@distractor-lu grouss
@distractor-lu hell
@distractor-lu bëlleg
@distractor-en big
@distractor-en bright
@distractor-en cheap

@fill
@lu De Computer ass [bëlleg] an d'Couche ass al.
@en The computer is [cheap] and the sofa is old.
@distractor-lu grouss
@distractor-lu nei
@distractor-lu kuerz
@distractor-en big
@distractor-en new
@distractor-en short

@fill
@lu De Pullover ass [rout] an d'Box ass schwaarz.
@en The jumper is [red] and the pants are black.
@distractor-lu blo
@distractor-lu gréng
@distractor-lu giel
@distractor-en blue
@distractor-en green
@distractor-en yellow

# --- @fill: question words ----------------------------------------------------
# Wou/Wat/Wéi/Wéini confusion is a genuine A1 pain point. The blank is always
# sentence-initial so no Eifeler-Regel risk.

@fill
@lu [Wou] ass d'Buedzëmmer?
@en [Where] is the bathroom?
@distractor-lu Wat
@distractor-lu Wéi
@distractor-lu Wéini
@distractor-en What
@distractor-en How
@distractor-en When

@fill
@lu [Wat] ass dat op dem Dësch?
@en [What] is that on the table?
@distractor-lu Wou
@distractor-lu Wéi
@distractor-lu Wéini
@distractor-en Where
@distractor-en How
@distractor-en When

@fill
@lu [Wéi] ass de Pullover?
@en [How] is the jumper?
@distractor-lu Wat
@distractor-lu Wou
@distractor-lu Wéini
@distractor-en What
@distractor-en Where
@distractor-en When

@fill
@lu [Wéini] reent et?
@en [When] does it rain?
@distractor-lu Wou
@distractor-lu Wat
@distractor-lu Wéi
@distractor-en Where
@distractor-en What
@distractor-en How

# --- @fill: prepositions and contractions -------------------------------------
# Prepositions zu/beim/an/op from sentences already taught in A1.01-A1.03.
# Determiners stay in the frame so the correct text is tile-independent.

@fill
@lu D'Couche ass [an] der Stuff.
@en The sofa is [in] the living room.
@distractor-lu op
@distractor-lu bei
@distractor-lu aus
@distractor-en on
@distractor-en near
@distractor-en from

@fill
@lu De Kaffi ass [op] dem Dësch.
@en The coffee is [on] the table.
@distractor-lu an
@distractor-lu bei
@distractor-lu aus
@distractor-en in
@distractor-en near
@distractor-en from

@fill
@lu Ech si [beim] Computer.
@en I am [at the] computer.
@distractor-lu um
@distractor-lu am
@distractor-lu aus dem
@distractor-en on the
@distractor-en in the
@distractor-en from the
